    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a572610e_3de9ba73",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/fair.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4017,
      "author": {
        "id": 1191469
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-13T13:43:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The tasks ignore/not ignore status can change over time as a consequence of the sched_slice() size and how long the task runs at each activation (wake-up to sleep). That is the goal.\nA task that ran a short amount of time at last activation will be ignored at the next wake-up. If it happens to run longer next time, it may be un-ignored at the tick-check. At the next activation it will start un-ignored. We just established in the other comment thread that a task shouldn\u0027t be ignored if it woke up as un-ignored. The only way for it to be ignored is to have a short activation cause the subsequent activation to give it ignore status.",
      "parentUuid": "61cff05e_14fb04d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4017,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 4017,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "e59064cc8bdb0b3f848773efe8a1ab2ae102edde",
